      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "There was plenty to like about the latest effort of VALENTINI (1) when she drew much wider and did some work but stuck on well at Leeton, beaten only 1.4 metres into second. She is well served by the inside draw. TIGER CHEDDAR (7) has been hard to fault of late having made it two wins in a row at this circuit and distance when he came from one spot wider at his latest appearance, getting home by 2.2 metres. Had enough speed to lead in both of those wins so can overcome another wide draw. ROLL THE ACES (4) recorded back-to-back wins last month, one of them at this circuit and distance, and has been solid since including a placing from a wider draw on Friday. MISS HERMES (3) draws well and is in the mix off a last-start win over VALENTINI at Leeton.",
